 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nFunctionDef.is_abstract() not detecting @abc.abstractmethod and @abc.abstractproperty decorators\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `is_abstract()` method on `FunctionDef` nodes is not properly detecting methods decorated with `@abc.abstractmethod` or `@abc.abstractproperty`. Methods that should be identified as abstract are returning `False` instead of `True`.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport astroid\n\ncode = '''\nimport abc\n\nclass Klass(object):\n    @abc.abstractproperty\n    def prop(self):\n       pass\n\n    @abc.abstractmethod\n    def method1(self):\n       pass\n'''\n\nmodule = astroid.parse(code)\nklass = module.body[1]\nprop = klass.body[0]\nmethod1 = klass.body[1]\n\nprint(f\"prop.is_abstract(): {prop.is_abstract(pass_is_abstract=False)}\")  # Expected: True, Actual: False\nprint(f\"method1.is_abstract(): {method1.is_abstract(pass_is_abstract=False)}\")  # Expected: True, Actual: False\n```\n\nExpected output:\n```\nprop.is_abstract(): True\nmethod1.is_abstract(): True\n```\n\nActual output:\n```\nprop.is_abstract(): False\nmethod1.is_abstract(): False\n```\n\nThe `is_abstract()` method should return `True` for functions decorated with `@abc.abstractmethod` or `@abc.abstractproperty`, but it's currently not detecting these decorators properly.\n</issue>\n",
